ideally i wanted it to rain but it's not  raining it's sunny so the closest thing  i can think of  [Music]  hello everyone my name is nori and  lately i've been writing these short  pieces based on your requests this week  i chose to write one inspired by the  prelude from maurice revels lutombo de  cupra  thank you to camilo for submitting this  idea so the first thing for me to do was  to learn the prelude which was really  great because i've actually been wanting  to learn it for a very long time but i  never got around to doing so until now  [Music]  without getting too caught up in the  details i focused on the different  things i love about this movement in a  broad sense  some of these include the figure eight  like pattern that creates a kind of  perpetual motion throughout the piece  the charming mortons that add a magical  touch and the circular progressions that  give the piece an unstable yet content  feel  just some notes about this keyboard  first of all for those of you who've  been commenting about the hidden piano  function yes i did know about it and i  use it pretty often but a lot of times i  choose to use the other sounds because  it's just very hard to get used to this  piano sound with this touch  it sounds like this by the way  [Music]  and  another thing about this keyboard is  that there is very very little  resistance  and that's okay if you're used to it but  i'm used to the weight of an upright or  a grand piano and with that comes some  habits such as me resting my my hands  and my fingers on the keys while i'm  playing between  bits where i'm playing and when i do  that on this keyboard sometimes it's too  much and i end up pressing the notes  so a lot of fast passages are very  difficult on this keyboard  and leaps as well  let me see what else um  i have a petal  made by yamaha  i just have one of these smaller ones  that i use  and that is about  it  and now here's the piece  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  [Music]  thanks so much for watching follow the  link in the description to find the  sheet music to this piece along with  some of my other works in written form  thank you so much for the support and  i'll see you in the next video  [Music]  you
 

